---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: false
scene: true
description: "John Carl Dimatulac builds full-stack applications, WordPress platforms, and automation systems."
---
<section class="studio-hero shell">
<div class="studio-copy"><p class="overline">John Carl Dimatulac / Full-stack developer</p><h1>Built to work.<br><span>Made to move.</span></h1><p class="studio-intro">I build web applications, WordPress platforms, and automation that keep everyday operations moving.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" class="btn" data-open-diagnostic>Analyze my website ↗</button><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Explore my work ↗</a></div></div>
<div class="system-stage" data-system-stage><div class="system-viewport" data-system-canvas aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="system-fallback" data-system-fallback aria-hidden="true"><span>INTERFACE</span><span>API</span><span>AUTOMATION</span><span>DATA</span></div><div class="scene-toolbar"><span>Inside the system</span><button type="button" class="motion-toggle" data-motion-toggle hidden aria-pressed="false">Pause motion</button></div><div class="layer-controls" role="group" aria-label="Explore the system layers"><button type="button" data-layer="0" aria-pressed="true">Interface</button><button type="button" data-layer="1" aria-pressed="false">API</button><button type="button" data-layer="2" aria-pressed="false">Automation</button><button type="button" data-layer="3" aria-pressed="false">Data</button></div><p class="layer-description" data-layer-description aria-live="polite">Interfaces people use. React, Next.js, and WordPress.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="selected-work"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Selected work</p><h2>Real projects.<br>Every layer considered.</h2><p>Client work, working demos, and independent concepts. Each with a clear role and a closer look at the build.</p></div><div class="project-showcase">{% for project in portfolio | slice_first(3) %}<article class="project-feature" data-enter><a class="project-image" href="/work/{{ project.slug }}/" aria-label="Explore {{ project.title }} case study"><img src="/assets/img/projects/{{ project.image }}.webp" width="{{ project.imageWidth }}" height="{{ project.imageHeight }}" alt="{{ project.title }} website homepage" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="project-caption"><div><p class="project-type">{{ project.kind }} / {{ project.field }}</p><h3><a href="/work/{{ project.slug }}/">{{ project.title }} ↗</a></h3></div><p>{{ project.summary }}</p></div></article>{% endfor %}</div><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Explore all {{ portfolio.length }} projects ↗</a></section>
<section class="pipeline-section" id="automation"><div class="shell"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Automation in practice</p><h2>From an idea<br>to a published article.</h2><p>A walkthrough of the n8n publishing pipeline I built for Spade. Select a stage to see its role.</p></div><div class="pipeline" role="group" aria-label="Publishing workflow stages"><button type="button" data-pipeline="0" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span><strong>Research</strong><small>Find the context</small></button><button type="button" data-pipeline="1" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span><strong>Write</strong><small>Shape the article</small></button><button type="button" data-pipeline="2" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span><strong>Optimize</strong><small>Prepare for search</small></button><button type="button" data-pipeline="3" aria-pressed="false"><span>04</span><strong>Publish</strong><small>Deliver to WordPress</small></button></div><div class="pipeline-detail"><p data-pipeline-description aria-live="polite">The Researcher stage gathers context for the article and passes it to the writing stage.</p><button class="text-link" type="button" data-play-pipeline>Play walkthrough ↗</button></div><p class="fine-print">Illustrated workflow. This walkthrough does not generate or publish content.</p></div></section>
<section class="portfolio-section shell capabilities" id="diagnostic-system"><div><p class="overline">System Diagnostic Protocol v1.0</p><h2>Website<br>diagnostic <span>system.</span></h2><p class="studio-intro">Enter a public website and the diagnostic reads its structure in the browser, then maps where the operation behind it is likely to break. Built into this site; no account needed.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" class="btn" data-open-diagnostic>Analyze my website ↗</button><a class="text-link" href="/work/lracdimension/">How it is built ↗</a></div></div><div class="capability-list" role="list" aria-label="What the diagnostic checks">{% for step in method %}<article role="listitem"><p class="project-type">{{ loop.index0 | pad }} / {{ step.status }}</p><h3>{{ step.title }}</h3><p>{{ step.desc }}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div></section>
<section class="portfolio-section shell capabilities"><div><h2>The interface.<br>The engine.<br><span>The connection.</span></h2><a class="text-link" href="/services/">How I can help ↗</a></div><div class="capability-list"><article><h3>Full-stack applications</h3><p>React and TypeScript interfaces connected to Node.js, PHP, and database-backed services.</p></article><article><h3>WordPress development</h3><p>Custom plugins, themes, REST API integrations, and content workflows.</p></article><article><h3>Automation & AI</h3><p>n8n pipelines, connected tools, AI-assisted publishing, and message automation.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="portfolio-section shell about-preview"><p class="overline">The person behind the systems</p><h2>I'm John Carl.<br>I connect the pieces.</h2><p>My background spans web development, construction IT, and network administration. I bring that operational perspective to every application I build.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Experience and approach ↗</a></section>
<section class="portfolio-section shell" id="research"><div class="section-title"><p class="overline">Research</p><h2>Notes from<br>the field.</h2><p>Articles on AI, web development, and how the two are changing the work. Sourced, dated, and written to be read in a few minutes.</p></div><div class="research-strip">{% for post in collections.research | sort(false, false, "data.order") | slice_first(3) %}<article data-enter>{% if post.data.image %}<a class="note-thumb" href="{{ post.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="{{ post.data.image }}" alt="" width="1024" height="572" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a>{% endif %}<p class="project-type">{{ post.data.topic }} / {{ post.templateContent | reading_time }} min read</p><h3><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></h3><p>{{ post.data.description }}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div><a class="text-link" href="/research/">All research ↗</a></section>
{% include "partials/studio-contact.njk" %}
